## Where the files go

| Item             | Location                                                           |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Recordings       | `~/Music/WRMC/`                                                    |
| Log file         | `~/Music/WRMC/recorder.log`                                        |
| Program          | `~/Library/Application Support/WRMC/wrmc.py`                       |
| Current schedule | `~/Library/Application Support/WRMC/schedule.json`                 |
| `wrmc` command   | `~/.local/bin/wrmc`                                                |
| Daily check      | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.murch.wrmc.update.plist`               |
| One recording    | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.murch.wrmc.show.<date>.<show>.plist`   |
| One alert        | `~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.murch.wrmc.remind.<date>.<show>.plist` |

### Recording file names

Each recording has the show name and the show date (New York date). For example:

- `TrailMix_2026-10-31.m4a`
- `TAM_2026-11-01.m4a`

If a file with the same name is already there, the tool adds the time to the new name. It does not write over a recording.

The files are AAC audio in an `.m4a` container. They play in Apple Music, QuickTime, VLC, and on iPhone. Each file has the show name, the date, and "WRMC 91.1 FM" in its information, so Apple Music sorts them well.

