## Troubleshooting

### First, look at the log

Most problems show in the log file. To see the last 30 lines, type:

```
tail -30 ~/Music/WRMC/recorder.log
```

Each line starts with the date and time. Look for lines with "FAILED", "WARNING", or "Could not".

### Keep the Mac awake

This is the most common cause of a missed recording. The Mac must be on and awake when the show starts.

- Keep the Mac plugged in to power.
- Keep the lid open. (A closed MacBook goes to sleep unless it has an external display.)
- In **System Settings > Battery > Options** (or **Energy**), turn on **"Prevent automatic sleeping on power adapter when the display is off"**.
- When the 12-hour alert comes, click **"Keep Mac awake until the show ends"**. If you do not answer the alert, the Mac stays awake anyway.

When a recording starts, the tool keeps the Mac awake until the recording stops.

If the Mac was asleep at the start time and wakes during the show, the tool records the rest of the show.

### The installer seems to stop or hang

- The Reminders step can take up to one minute. Wait for it.
- macOS can show a permission window behind the Terminal window. Look for it and click **OK**.
- If nothing happens after two minutes, press **Ctrl + C**. Then run the installer again. The recordings are set before the Reminders step, so they still work.

### "command not found: wrmc"

- Open a **new** Terminal window. Old windows do not know the new command.
- If it still fails, use the full command:

  ```
  python3 ~/Library/Application\ Support/WRMC/wrmc.py list
  ```

- Make sure that `~/.zshrc` has this line: `export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"`

### `wrmc list` shows no shows

1. Type `wrmc update` and read the result.
2. If you see "No shows by _name_ found", her shows are not on the schedule this week (for example, during a college break). The tool tries again each day.
3. If you see "Could not download schedule", see [The schedule does not download](#the-schedule-does-not-download).
4. If Avery's shows are on the website but the tool does not find them, the website may have changed its host tags. Open the schedule page, click her show, and look at the link on her name. Put the last part of that link in `HOST_TAGS`, or put the show names in `SHOW_TITLES`. See [Settings](#settings).

### The schedule does not download

- Make sure that the Mac is on the internet.
- Open <https://wrmc.middlebury.edu/schedule-weekly> in a browser to make sure that the site works.
- Try this command, which shows the size of the page:

  ```
  curl -sL https://wrmc.middlebury.edu/schedule-weekly | wc -c
  ```

  A number above 100000 is correct. A small number or an error means a network or site problem.

- If the download fails, the tool keeps the recordings that it already set.

### The test recording fails, or the file is empty

1. Make sure that ffmpeg is installed: `ffmpeg -version`. If not, type `brew install ffmpeg`.
2. Make sure that the stream works. Type this command. It records 10 seconds to your Desktop:

   ```
   ffmpeg -i https://us2.maindigitalstream.com/ssl/WRMC -t 10 -c copy ~/Desktop/stream_test.aac
   ```

3. If that fails, the stream address may have changed. Go to <https://wrmc.middlebury.edu>, click **Listen Now**, and find the new stream address (see [Find a new stream address](#find-a-new-stream-address)). Put it in `STREAM_URL` in `wrmc.py` and run the installer again.

### A show was not recorded

1. Look at the log: `tail -50 ~/Music/WRMC/recorder.log`
2. If there is no "Recording ..." line for that show:
   - The Mac was probably asleep or off. See [Keep the Mac awake](#keep-the-mac-awake).
   - Or the show was not set. Type `wrmc list` to see what is set now.
3. If there is a "Recording ..." line but the file is short:
   - The internet connection probably stopped. The tool tries to reconnect for 30 seconds. If the connection stops for longer, the recording ends early.
   - Look at the "ffmpeg exit code" in the "Finished" line. Code 0 is a good result.

### The recording starts or stops at the wrong time

- Make sure that the Mac has the correct time and time zone: **System Settings > General > Date & Time**. Turn on "Set time and date automatically".
- Type `wrmc list`. Compare the New York time with the schedule page.
- If you changed the time zone on the Mac, type `wrmc update`.

### No Apple Reminders items

- Open **System Settings > Privacy & Security > Automation**. Make sure that Terminal and python3 can control **Reminders**.
- The tool puts items in your **default** Reminders list. Look in that list.
- Look in the log for "Could not update Apple Reminders".
- If you do not want Reminders items, set `USE_APPLE_REMINDERS = False`. The Mac alert still works.

### No notifications

- Open **System Settings > Notifications**. Find **Script Editor** (macOS shows notifications from scripts with this name) and turn on **Allow notifications**.
- Make sure that Focus or Do Not Disturb is off.

### Old reminders or alerts for a show that moved

The daily check removes old items when the schedule changes. To do it now, type `wrmc update`.

### See what launchd has scheduled

To see all WRMC jobs that macOS knows about, type:

```
launchctl list | grep wrmc
```

You see one line for the daily check, one line for each recording, and one line for each alert.

### Find a new stream address

If the station changes its stream:

1. Open <https://wrmc.middlebury.edu> in Chrome and click **Listen Now**.
2. Press **Cmd + Option + I** to open the developer tools, then click **Network**.
3. Click play. Look for a request that continues to load (the audio stream). Often the address has "stream", "ssl", ".mp3", or ".aac" in it.
4. Right-click it and copy the URL. Put it in `STREAM_URL` in `wrmc.py`, and run the installer again.

### Start again from the beginning

```
wrmc uninstall
bash ~/build/wrmc_recorder/install_wrmc_recorder.sh
```

