## How it works

This section is for people who want to change the tool.

### Schedule

The schedule page has one `<article class="show-teaser">` element for each show. Each element has:

- Two `<time datetime="...">` elements: the start and end, with the time zone (for example `2026-10-31T09:00:00-0400`).
- An `<h3>` element with the show name.
- Links to `/tags/<host-name>` for each host.

Each show is on the page two times (in the grid and in the list). The tool removes the copies. It uses only the Python standard library to read the page.

### Scheduling

The tool uses **launchd**, which is the macOS system that starts jobs at set times. (macOS does not support time zones in cron, so cron is not a good choice.)

- `com.murch.wrmc.update` runs each day at 6:07 am and at login. It runs `wrmc.py update --quiet`.
- For each show, `com.murch.wrmc.show.*` runs at the start time minus 2 minutes, on that date. It runs `wrmc.py record`.
- For each show, `com.murch.wrmc.remind.*` runs 12 hours before. It runs `wrmc.py remind`.

The times in these jobs are in the Mac's local time. The tool calculates them again each day, so clock changes are always correct.

If the Mac is asleep at a job time, launchd runs the job when the Mac wakes. The record step then records the remaining part of the show. If the remaining time is less than one minute, it does not record.

The show jobs also run at login. The record step checks the time and records only if the show is on air or starts within 10 minutes. A lock file prevents two recordings of the same show.

### Recording

The tool uses ffmpeg to copy the stream with no change in quality:

```
caffeinate -i ffmpeg -reconnect 1 -reconnect_streamed 1 -reconnect_delay_max 30 \
  -i https://us2.maindigitalstream.com/ssl/WRMC -t <seconds> \
  -c copy -bsf:a aac_adtstoasc <file>.m4a
```

- `caffeinate -i` keeps the Mac awake during the recording.
- The `-reconnect` options try to connect again if the stream stops for a short time.
- `-c copy` saves the audio as it is, with no conversion.

### Stream

- Player page: `https://us7.maindigitalstream.com/4302/`
- Audio stream: `https://us2.maindigitalstream.com/ssl/WRMC` (type `audio/aacp`)

### Apple Reminders

The tool uses AppleScript to make the Reminders items. It reads the names of open reminders one time, adds the items that are not there, and deletes old items that start with "WRMC:". It saves a record of the last set of items, and it does not use the Reminders app if nothing has changed. This is because AppleScript access to Reminders is slow.

